  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Response to the Conflict Escalation through Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH), Basic Assistance (BA), and Shelter Intervention in South Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe project stands as a comprehensive and immediate response to address the pressing needs of internally displaced populations (IDPs) situated along the Southern border of Lebanon in proximity to the Occupied Palestinian Territory (OPT) as a result of the conflict escalation. This comprehensive initiative employs an integrated approach that covers Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH), Basic Assistance (BA), and Shelter activities. Recognizing the complexity of the situation, the project prioritizes and acknowledges the need for collaboration with governmental entities, United Nations (UN) agencies, and non-governmental organizations (NGOs). This strategic collaboration underscores the organization&apos;s unwavering commitment to localization, ensuring that interventions are contextually relevant and effectively implemented in turn creating a tangible and positive impact on the lives of those affected by displacement.ltbrgtIn line with the Lebanon National Response Plan and the sector-specific WASH, Shelter, and BA response plans, the project aims to address existing gaps in services and provide tailor-made assistance to the communities most severely affected. This includes those displaced to temporary shelters, newly established households, and residents of frontline villages, who are often exposed to heightened vulnerabilities.ltbrgtSave the Children, a prominent organization with a substantial presence in Lebanon has been actively delivering essential supplies and services since the onset of the conflict. The consistent and dedicated efforts underscore a commitment to a localized and comprehensive crisis response, ensuring that the assistance provided is both timely and meaningful. lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
